# See https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file for more about ignoring files.

# Ignore git directory.
/.git/
/.gitignore

# Ignore bundler config.
/.bundle

# Ignore all environment files.
/.env*

# Ignore all default key files.
/config/master.key
/config/credentials/*.key
# The encrypted credentials vault: ciphertext, but do NOT ship it into the PUBLIC
# GHCR image — a leaked RAILS_MASTER_KEY (plaintext in the job container env) would
# then decrypt it. secret_key_base comes from SECRET_KEY_BASE env at runtime, so
# the container never needs the .enc. Canon 06_04 §2.2.
/config/credentials.yml.enc

# Ignore all logfiles and tempfiles.
/log/*
/tmp/*
!/log/.keep
!/tmp/.keep

# Ignore pidfiles, but keep the directory.
/tmp/pids/*
!/tmp/pids/.keep

# Ignore storage (uploaded files in development and any SQLite databases).
/storage/*
!/storage/.keep
/tmp/storage/*
!/tmp/storage/.keep

# Ignore assets.
/node_modules/
/app/assets/builds/*
!/app/assets/builds/.keep
/public/assets

# Ignore CI service files.
/.github

# Ignore Kamal files.
/config/deploy*.yml
/.kamal

# Ignore Terraform — never part of the Rails image, and a local `terraform apply`
# renders terraform/*.tfvars with REAL secrets that a
# local `docker build .` / `kamal deploy` from the same cwd would otherwise bake
# into the PUBLIC image (structural gap; CI is fresh-checkout so not firing today).
/terraform

# Ignore development files
/.devcontainer

# [OPS.10] Trees the Rails runtime never reads — `COPY . .` shipped all of them
# into the PUBLIC GHCR image (see .github/workflows/mirror-ghcr.yml).
# Measured 2026-08-28 on the VERSIONED tree (what a CI fresh-checkout sees, not a
# local worktree with its build artifacts): 418 MB total, of which firmware 330 MB,
# tools 52 MB, docs 20 MB, spec 6.1 MB. Verified before cutting: nothing under
# app/ · lib/ · config/ READS these paths at runtime — the only hits are a message
# string, a rake-only glob and a generator output path.
# Sibling of BUNDLE_WITHOUT="development:test" above: that one keeps the test GEMS
# out, this one keeps the test and non-Rails SOURCE out. Closing only the first
# leaves the larger half in place while the item reads as done.
#
# ⛔ `/scripts` AND `/deploy` WERE DELIBERATELY *NOT* CUT, and the reason is recorded
# because a future sweep will otherwise re-open it as an oversight: both are versioned
# and small, so the risk of cutting — a rake task, an entrypoint or an accessory config
# reaching for a path that is no longer in the image, discovered at runtime rather than
# at build — exceeds the megabytes saved. The list above is what measurement JUSTIFIED
# cutting; absence from it is a decision, not a gap.
/spec
/docs
/firmware
/tools
/contracts
/subgraph
/.claude

# Local-only artifacts. Gitignored, so a CI fresh-checkout never has them — but a
# local `docker build .` / `kamal deploy` from the same cwd bakes them in, which is
# the identical structural gap already spelled out for /terraform above.
/coverage
/test

# Ignore Docker-related files
/.dockerignore
/Dockerfile*
